{
  "Name": "rConfig install Command Execution",
  "Description": "This module exploits an unauthenticated command injection vulnerability in rConfig versions 3.9.2 and prior. The `install` directory is not automatically removed after installation, allowing unauthenticated users to execute arbitrary commands via the `ajaxServerSettingsChk.php` file as the web server user. This module has been tested successfully on rConfig version 3.9.2 on CentOS 7.7.1908 (x64).",
